  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ARM: Armenian Democracy Watch: Monitoring Progress and Advocating for Change</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Democracy Watch will produce:   

Weekly Reports: A one-page report highlighting key recent events related to the project&apos;s identified topics, with commentary from experts. 

Monthly Summary: A comprehensive summary of developments from that month, presented in a video interview format on CivilNet. 

In-depth Articles: Commissioning in-depth articles to experts on democratic backsliding and democratic consolidation &#x2013;&#x2013; both theoretical and empirical, providing more detailed analysis and insights into specific topics. 

These reports will be presented on a dedicated page on CivilNet&#x2019;s website, offering factual insights and incorporating commentary from experts. Through this monitoring and analysis, Democracy Watch aims to shed light on the challenges facing Armenia&apos;s democratic development and encourage informed dialogue to address them. At the end of each month, these reports will be summarized in a video interview format by one of the experts conducting and writing the analysis. 

Research will be conducted by the Regional Center for Democracy and Security and distributed on CivilNet platforms, including the website, Facebook and X (500K and  35K followers respectively), Youtube (265K subscribers), etc. CivilNet will also use its Newsletter (100K subscribers) to reach the target audiences.  

Topics will be chosen using an established methodology, based on existing scholarship on democratic backsliding, best practices of international watchdog organizations, and Armenian legislation, ensuring a systematic approach to monitoring and analysis.</narrative>
  </description>
